{"cut_proposal":{"candidate_errors":[],"prefix":"To solve the problem, we need to find a base \\( b \\) such that the base-10 integers 36, 64, and 81 can all be represented by the same three-digit number \\(\\triangle\\Box\\Box\\) in base \\( b \\). This means that in base \\( b \\), the number \\(\\triangle\\Box\\Box\\) represents the same value in base-10 for each of these integers.\n\nThe number \\(\\triangle\\Box\\Box\\) in base \\( b \\) can be expressed in base-10 as:\n\\[\n\\triangle \\cdot b^2 + \\Box \\cdot b + \\Box = \\triangle \\cdot b^2 + 2\\Box \\cdot b\n\\]\nWe need this expression to be equal to 36, 64, and 81 for some digits \\(\\triangle\\) and \\(\\Box\\) in base \\( b \\).\n\nFirst, let's check the possible range for \\( b \\). Since \\(\\triangle\\Box\\Box\\) is a three-digit number in base \\( b \\), it must satisfy:\n\\[\nb^2 \\leq 36 < b^3\n\\]\nFrom \\( b^2 \\leq 36 \\), we get \\( b \\leq 6 \\). From \\( 36 < b^3 \\), we get \\( b > 3 \\). Therefore, the possible values for \\( b \\) are 4, 5, and 6.\n\nLet's check each case:\n\n1. **Base \\( b = 4 \\):**\n   \\[\n   b^2 = 16, \\quad 2b = 8\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   \\triangle \\cdot 16 + 2 \\cdot 4 = 36 \\implies 16\\triangle + 8 = 36 \\implies 16\\triangle = 28 \\implies \\triangle = \\frac{28}{16} = 1.75 \\quad (\\text{not an integer})\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   \\triangle \\cdot 16 + 2 \\cdot 4 = 64 \\implies 16\\triangle + 8 = 64 \\implies 16\\triangle = 56 \\implies \\triangle = \\frac{56}{16} = 3.5 \\quad (\\text{not an integer})\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   \\triangle \\cdot 16 + 2 \\cdot 4 = 81 \\implies 16\\triangle + 8 = 81 \\implies 16\\triangle = 73 \\implies \\triangle = \\frac{73}{16} = 4.5625 \\quad (\\text{not an integer})\n   \\]\n   So, base 4 does not work.\n\n2. **Base \\( b = 5 \\):**\n   \\[\n   b^2 = 25, \\quad 2b = 10\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   \\triangle \\cdot 25 + 2 \\cdot 5 = 36 \\implies 25\\triangle + 10 = 36 \\implies 25\\triangle = 26 \\implies \\triangle = \\frac{26}{25} = 1.04 \\quad (\\text{not an integer})\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   \\triangle \\cdot 25 + 2 \\cdot 5 = 64 \\implies 25\\triangle + 10 = 64 \\implies 25\\triangle = 54 \\implies \\triangle = \\frac{54}{25} = 2.16 \\quad (\\text{not an integer})\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   \\triangle \\cdot 25 + 2 \\cdot 5 = 81 \\implies 25\\triangle + 10 = 81 \\implies 25\\triangle = 71 \\implies \\triangle = \\frac{71}{25} = 2.84 \\quad (\\text{not an integer})\n   \\]\n   So, base 5 does not work.\n\n","prefix_end":2205,"status":"review_required"},"eligible":true,"generation":{"generation":{"max_new_tokens":2048,"temperature":0.7,"top_k":0,"top_p":1.0},"ids":[1249,11625,279,3491,11,582,1184,311,1477,264,2331,17767,293,1124,8,1741,429,279,2331,12,16,15,25780,220,18,21,11,220,21,19,11,323,220,23,16,646,678,387,15251,553,279,1852,2326,48342,1372,1124,11520,55114,59,1611,59,1611,57758,304,2331,17767,293,1124,568,1096,3363,429,304,2331,17767,293,1124,701,279,1372,1124,11520,55114,59,1611,59,1611,57758,10868,279,1852,897,304,2331,12,16,15,369,1817,315,1493,25780,382,785,1372,1124,11520,55114,59,1611,59,1611,57758,304,2331,17767,293,1124,8,646,387,13302,304,2331,12,16,15,438,510,59,9640,59,55114,1124,50853,293,61,17,488,1124,1611,1124,50853,293,488,1124,1611,284,1124,55114,1124,50853,293,61,17,488,220,17,59,1611,1124,50853,293,198,59,921,1654,1184,419,7493,311,387,6144,311,220,18,21,11,220,21,19,11,323,220,23,16,369,1045,18509,1124,11520,55114,57758,323,1124,11520,1611,57758,304,2331,17767,293,1124,3593,5338,11,1077,594,1779,279,3204,2088,369,17767,293,1124,568,8704,1124,11520,55114,59,1611,59,1611,57758,374,264,2326,48342,1372,304,2331,17767,293,1124,701,432,1969,26553,510,59,9640,65,61,17,1124,273,80,220,18,21,366,293,61,18,198,59,921,3830,17767,293,61,17,1124,273,80,220,18,21,1124,701,582,633,17767,293,1124,273,80,220,21,1124,568,5542,17767,220,18,21,366,293,61,18,1124,701,582,633,17767,293,861,220,18,1124,568,15277,11,279,3204,2750,369,17767,293,1124,8,525,220,19,11,220,20,11,323,220,21,382,10061,594,1779,1817,114